=== REAL gem bytes verified in each image (`ruby -e 'require "faraday"; puts Faraday::VERSION'`) ===
  v0 image -> faraday 2.14.0   (pre CVE-2026-25765; protocol-relative host override open for String AND URI)
  v1 image -> faraday 2.14.1   (CVE-2026-25765 fix: STRING //host re-scoped; URI object still overrides = TARGET)
  v2 image -> faraday 2.14.2   (CVE-2026-33637 fix: `url = url.to_s if url.respond_to?(:host)`; connection.rb byte-identical in 2.14.3)

=== The real sink: Faraday::Connection#build_exclusive_url (lib/faraday/connection.rb) ===
  2.14.0:  url = "./#{url}" if url.respond_to?(:start_with?) && !url.start_with?('http://','https://','/','./','../')
           -> a protocol-relative target starts with '/', so the ./-guard does NOT fire -> URI#merge takes //authority -> host override.
  2.14.1:  url = "./#{url}" if url.respond_to?(:start_with?) &&
                              (!url.start_with?('http://','https://','/','./','../') || url.start_with?('//'))
           -> a STRING //host is now ./-prefixed (blocked); BUT a URI object does NOT respond_to?(:start_with?) -> guard skipped -> host override (RESIDUAL).
  2.14.2:  url = url.to_s if url.respond_to?(:host)   # <-- coerces URI object to its String form FIRST
           url = "./#{url}" if url.respond_to?(:start_with?) && (url.start_with?('//') || !url.start_with?(...))
           -> URI object now goes through the //-guard -> ./-prefixed (blocked).

=== Harness (faithful-core, one image per version, three ROLEs) ===
  ROLE=base     trusted-base.pcb  -> serves "TRUSTED-BASE OK ..." on any path (the configured base URL host; NOT the flag)
  ROLE=attacker attacker.pcb      -> serves ${PCB_FLAG} on any path; NO published host port (internal-only canary)
  ROLE=server   Faraday.new(url:'http://trusted-base.pcb').get(target); GET /fetch?to=<t>&mode=<string|uri>
                  mode=string -> conn.get(t)         (raw String; original CVE-2026-25765 channel)
                  mode=uri    -> conn.get(URI(t))    (app parses input into a URI object; CVE-2026-33637 channel)
  ports: server-v0=39610, server-v1=39611, server-v2=39612 (base+attacker have NO host port)

